course: dictionary
lesson: 11611
title: Appreciation: thanks, enjoyment and value
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: «Appreciation» is a noun with more than one meaning, so the words around it show you which one fits. «She wrote a card to show her appreciation for the help.» Here appreciation means thanks.
explain: «The class listened with real appreciation to the orchestra.» Nobody is thanking anyone here. The children understood and enjoyed how good the music was. Always ask: what would fit in this sentence? Try "thanks" or "enjoyment" and see which one still makes sense.
explain: Two more meanings. «The teacher showed an appreciation of how hard the problem was.» That means understanding a situation. In money talk, «The house gained a lot in appreciation over ten years» means its value went up. Same word, different jobs: check the clues before you choose.
fact: Appreciation means thanks or gratitude for something.
fact: Appreciation can also mean understanding and enjoying how good something is, as in «art appreciation».
fact: Appreciation can mean understanding of a situation, or a rise in the value of something, such as a house or a coin.
fact: Useful phrases are «in appreciation of» and «show appreciation».
fact: A good check is to swap in "thanks" or "enjoyment" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «She gave the nurse a box of chocolates to show her appreciation.» What does appreciation mean here? | Falling asleep | *Thanks | Shouting loudly | Being rude
exercise: «The art class spent the afternoon in appreciation of the paintings, enjoying every colour.» What does appreciation mean here? | A rise in price | *Enjoying and understanding how good something is | Being bored by something | Thanks for a present
exercise: «Over ten years, the house gained a lot in appreciation.» What does appreciation mean here? | *A rise in value | Tidying up the garden | Being sad and tired | Thanks and gratitude
test: «Thank you so much for the lovely present. My appreciation is huge.» What does appreciation mean here? | Shouting at a friend | Being very tired | A fall in price | *Thanks and gratitude
test: «The teacher explained the problem, and now I have an appreciation of why it was so hard.» What does appreciation mean here? | A rise in money | *Understanding of a situation | Thanks for the lesson | Being noisy in class
exam: Which phrase means you are thanking someone for a gift? | *In appreciation of your gift | A rise in price | Fallen autumn leaves | A field of corn
